### Goal Model Decomposition

#### Goal Nodes

| Goal ID | Title | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|--------|-------|------|---------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1     | Manage Food Delivery and Dish Retrieval | Manage the delivery of food and retrieval of dirty dishes in the hospital. | - | Achieve | - | Root goal for the mission. |
| G2     | Deliver Food | Deliver food from the kitchen to the inpatient room. | ; (Sequential) | Perform | AND | Both food delivery and tracking are necessary. |
| G3     | Retrieve Dishes | Retrieve dirty dishes from the inpatient room. | ; (Sequential) | Perform | AND | Both dish retrieval and door handling are necessary. |
| G2.1   | Deliver Food to Room | Deliver food to the inpatient room. | - | Achieve | AND | Essential for providing food. |
| G2.2   | Track Meal Retrieval | Track when and where each meal is retrieved. | - | Achieve | AND | Ensures correct meal delivery. |
| G2.3   | Alert Wrong Meal | Alert if a wrong meal is retrieved. | - | Achieve | AND | Prevents errors in meal delivery. |
| G3.1   | Retrieve Dishes | Retrieve dirty dishes from the room. | - | Achieve | AND | Necessary for cleaning. |
| G3.2   | Handle Door Opening | Open the room door. | - | Achieve | AND | Required for access. |
| G3.3   | Respond to Calls | Respond to calls from the room. | - | Achieve | AND | Ensures responsiveness. |

#### Task Nodes

| Task ID | Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|-------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| AT2.1   | Deliver Food | Deliver food to the inpatient room. | AND | Hospital Room | 1 | Single robot for delivery. |
| AT2.2   | Track Meals | Track meal retrieval details. | AND | Hospital Room | 1 | Single robot for tracking. |
| AT2.3   | Alert Wrong Meal | Alert if the wrong meal is taken. | AND | Hospital Room | 1 | Single robot for alerting. |
| AT3.1   | Retrieve Dishes | Collect dirty dishes from the room. | AND | Hospital Room | 1 | Single robot for retrieval. |
| AT3.2.1 | Open Door with Robot | Open door using a robot. | OR | Hospital Room | 1 | Alternative method. |
| AT3.2.2 | Open Door with Human | Open door with human assistance. | OR | Hospital Room | 1 | Alternative method. |
| AT3.3.1 | Respond to Robot Call | Answer call from a robot. | OR | Hospital Room | 1 | Alternative response. |
| AT3.3.2 | Respond to Human Call | Answer call from a human. | OR | Hospital Room | 1 | Alternative response. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both food delivery and dish retrieval are essential for the mission.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2, G2.3 [AND]**  
  Justification: All steps are necessary for successful food delivery.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2, G3.3 [AND]**  
  Justification: All steps are necessary for successful dish retrieval.

- **G2.1 -> AT2.1, AT2.2, AT2.3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Each task is required for delivering food correctly.

- **G3.2 -> AT3.2.1, AT3.2.2 [OR]**  
  Justification: Either a robot or a human can open the door.

- **G3.3 -> AT3.3.1, AT3.3.2 [OR]**  
  Justification: Either a robot or a human can respond to the call.

This structured approach ensures that all aspects of the mission are covered, with clear relationships and justifications for each step.
